# Respiratory Disease Hospitalization Forecasting Using Air Pollution Data

### Environmental Health Analytics & Machine Learning Forecasting

This notebook develops an end-to-end machine learning workflow for forecasting daily respiratory disease hospitalizations using environmental, demographic, and temporal indicators.

The analysis investigates whether air pollution and environmental conditions can help anticipate changes in respiratory healthcare demand and identifies the factors that contribute most strongly to hospitalization forecasts.

**Primary objectives**

* Explore environmental and hospitalization patterns.
* Quantify relationships between air pollution and respiratory hospitalizations.
* Engineer temporal and lag-based forecasting features.
* Train a Random Forest regression model.
* Evaluate forecasting performance using MAE, RMSE, and R².
* Identify important environmental and historical predictors.
* Generate future hospitalization forecasts.
* Translate analytical findings into public-health planning insights.

> **Disclaimer:** The dataset used in this project is synthetic and is intended for educational, research, and portfolio-development purposes. It does not contain real patient information and should not be used for clinical decision-making.

